Polyhedra -- for computations with convex polyhedra, cones, and fans
********************************************************************

Description
===========

A rational convex *note Polyhedron: Polyhedron, is the intersection of finitely
many affine half-spaces over *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ, or equivalently, the
convex hull of a finite set of vertices and rays. A rational convex polyhedral
*note Cone: Cone, is the intersection of finitely many linear half-spaces over
*note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ, or equivalently, the positive hull of a finite set
of rays. A *note Fan: Fan, is a finite collection of cones such that for each
cone all its faces are in the fan and for two cones in the fan the intersection
is a face of each.


Polyhedra uses the 
  * *note FourierMotzkin: (FourierMotzkin)Top, package by Gregory G. Smith (see
    http://www.mast.queensu.ca/~ggsmith )
  * *note FourTiTwo: (FourTiTwo)Top, package by Michael Stillman (see
    http://pi.math.cornell.edu/~mike/ ), Josephine Yu (see
    http://people.math.gatech.edu/~jyu67/ ), and Sonja Petrovic (see
    http://math.iit.edu/~spetrov1/ )
  * *note Normaliz: (Normaliz)Top, package by Gesa Kaempf and Christof Soeger
  * *note Topcom: (Topcom)Top, package by Michael Stillman (see
    http://pi.math.cornell.edu/~mike/ ).


Here are some examples illustrating the main uses of this package.
  * *note Working with polyhedra: Working with polyhedra,
  * *note Working with cones: Working with cones,
  * *note Working with fans: Working with fans,


Please have a look at *note V- and H-representation: V- and H-representation,
on conventions used throughout this package before you start.


For an introduction to polyhedra and cones, we recommend Gunter M. Ziegler's
(see http://www.mi.fu-berlin.de/math/groups/discgeom/ziegler/ ) Lectures on
Polytopes, Graduate Texts in Mathematics 152, Springer-Verlag, New York, 1995.


