affineImage(Matrix,Cone,Matrix) -- computes the affine image of a cone
**********************************************************************

  * Function: *note affineImage: affineImage,
  * Usage: 
        C1 = affineImage(A,C,b) 
        C1 = affineImage(A,C) 
        C1 = affineImage(C,b)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,,  with entries in *note ZZ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * b, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,,  with entries in *note ZZ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ, and only one column
        representing a vector
  * Outputs:
      * C1, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,,  of class *note Cone: Cone,
        or *note Polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


A must be a matrix from the ambient space of the cone C to some other target
space and b must be a vector in that target space, i.e. the number of columns
of A must equal the ambient dimension of C and A and b must have the same
number of rows. Then affineImage computes the polyhedron {(A*c)+b | c in C} and
the cone {A*c | c in C} if b is 0 or omitted. If A is omitted then it is set to
identity.


For example, consider the following three dimensional cone.
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2,3},{3,1,2},{2,3,1}}|
|                                                       |
|o1 = C                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o1 : Cone                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+


This Cone can be mapped to the positive orthant:
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = matrix  {{-5,7,1},{1,-5,7},{7,1,-5}}|
|                                             |
|o2 = | -5 7  1  |                            |
|     | 1  -5 7  |                            |
|     | 7  1  -5 |                            |
|                                             |
|              3       3                      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                       |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C1 = affineImage(A,C)                   |
|                                             |
|o3 = C1                                      |
|                                             |
|o3 : Cone                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rays C1                                 |
|                                             |
|o4 = | 1 0 0 |                               |
|     | 0 1 0 |                               |
|     | 0 0 1 |                               |
|                                             |
|              3       3                      |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                       |
+---------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "affineImage(Cone,Matrix)"
  * "affineImage(Matrix,Cone)"
  * *note affineImage(Matrix,Cone,Matrix):
    affineImage_lpMatrix_cmCone_cmMatrix_rp, -- computes the affine image of a
    cone
