commonFace -- checks if the intersection is a face of both Cones or Polyhedra, or of cones with fans
****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b = commonFace(C1,C2) 
        b = commonFace(P1,P2) 
        b = commonFace(X,F) 
        b = commonFace(F,X) 
        b = commonFace L
  * Inputs:
      * C1, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * C2, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * P1, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
      * P2, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
      * F, an instance of the type *note Fan: Fan,
      * X, *note Cone: Cone, or *note Fan: Fan,
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if the intersection is a face both, and *note
        false: (Macaulay2Doc)false, otherwise.

Description
===========


commonFace checks if the intersection of C1 and C2 or the intersection of P1
and P2 is a face of both. If it is applied to a pair of a cone C and a fan F
then it checks if the intersection of C with every generating cone of F is a
face of each. For two fans it checks this condition for every pair of
generating cones. If applied to a list then the list must contain Fans and
Cones and it checks pairwise for a common face.


For example, consider the following three cones:
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,0},{0,1}};  |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,-1},{0,-1}};|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C3 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,-1},{2,-1}};|
+-----------------------------------------------+


for each pair of two of them we can check if their intersection is a common
face:
+----------------------+
|i4 : commonFace(C1,C2)|
|                      |
|o4 = true             |
+----------------------+
|i5 : commonFace(C2,C3)|
|                      |
|o5 = true             |
+----------------------+
|i6 : commonFace(C3,C1)|
|                      |
|o6 = false            |
+----------------------+

Ways to use commonFace:
=======================

  * "commonFace(Cone,Cone)"
  * "commonFace(Cone,Fan)"
  * "commonFace(Fan,Cone)"
  * "commonFace(Fan,Fan)"
  * "commonFace(List)"
  * "commonFace(Polyhedron,Polyhedron)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note commonFace: commonFace, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

