Cone * Cone -- computes the direct product of two cones
*******************************************************

  * Operator: *note *: (Macaulay2Doc)_st,
  * Usage: 
        C = C1 * C2
  * Inputs:
      * C1, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * C2, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,

Description
===========


Computes the direct product of C1 and C2. This is the cone {(x,y) | x in C1, y
in C2}, in the direct product of the ambient spaces.


See also *note directProduct(Cone,Cone): directProduct_lpCone_cmCone_rp,.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2},{2,1}}|
|                                            |
|o1 = C1                                     |
|                                            |
|o1 : Cone                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix {{1}}        |
|                                            |
|o2 = C2                                     |
|                                            |
|o2 : Cone                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = C1 * C2                            |
|                                            |
|o3 = C                                      |
|                                            |
|o3 : Cone                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rays C                                 |
|                                            |
|o4 = | 2 1 0 |                              |
|     | 1 2 0 |                              |
|     | 0 0 1 |                              |
|                                            |
|              3       3                     |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                      |
+--------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Cone * Cone: Cone _st Cone, -- computes the direct product of two
    cones
