Cone * Polyhedron -- computes the direct product of a cone and a polyhedron
***************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note *: (Macaulay2Doc)_st,
  * Usage: 
        Q = C * P
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
  * Outputs:
      * Q, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


Computes the direct product of C and P. This is the polyhedron {(c,p) | c in C,
p in P}, in the direct product of the ambient spaces.


See also *note directProduct(Cone,Cone): directProduct_lpCone_cmCone_rp,.
+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2},{2,1}}|
|                                           |
|o1 = C                                     |
|                                           |
|o1 : Cone                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P =convexHull matrix {{1},{-1}}       |
|                                           |
|o2 = P                                     |
|                                           |
|o2 : Polyhedron                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = C * P                             |
|                                           |
|o3 = Q                                     |
|                                           |
|o3 : Polyhedron                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (vertices Q,rays Q)                   |
|                                           |
|o4 = (| 0  |, | 2 1 |)                     |
|      | 0  |  | 1 2 |                      |
|      | 1  |  | 0 0 |                      |
|      | -1 |  | 0 0 |                      |
|                                           |
|o4 : Sequence                              |
+-------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

