Cone + Cone -- computes the Minkowski sum of two cones
******************************************************

  * Operator: *note +: (Macaulay2Doc)+,
  * Usage: 
        C = C1 + C2
  * Inputs:
      * C1, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * C2, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,

Description
===========


Computes the Minkowski sum of C1 and C2. This is the cone C1 + C2 = {x + y | x
in C1, y in C2}. Note that C1 and C2 have to lie in the same ambient space.


See also *note minkowskiSum: minkowskiSum,.
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2,3},{2,3,1},{3,1,2}}|
|                                                        |
|o1 = C1                                                 |
|                                                        |
|o1 : Cone                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix {{1},{0},{0}}            |
|                                                        |
|o2 = C2                                                 |
|                                                        |
|o2 : Cone                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = C1 + C2                                        |
|                                                        |
|o3 = C                                                  |
|                                                        |
|o3 : Cone                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rays C                                             |
|                                                        |
|o4 = | 1 2 3 1 |                                        |
|     | 0 3 1 2 |                                        |
|     | 0 1 2 3 |                                        |
|                                                        |
|              3       4                                 |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

