Cone ? Cone -- compares the Cones
*********************************

  * Operator: *note ?: (Macaulay2Doc)?,
  * Usage: 
        b = C1 ? C2
  * Inputs:
      * C1, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * C2, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, > or < or =

Description
===========


This induces an order on Cones. C1 is greater then C2 if its ambient dimension
is greater, if this is equal then if its dimension is higher and if this is
equal if it has the higher ordered rays and lineality space.
