crossPolytope -- computes the d-dimensional crosspolytope with diameter 2s
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        P = crossPolytope(d,s)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,  strictly positive
      * s, *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, positive
        (optional)
  * Outputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


The d-dimensional crossPolytope with diameter s is the convex hull of +/- s
times the standard basis in *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,^d. If s is omitted it
is set to 1.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : P = crossPolytope(3,3/2)      |
|                                   |
|o1 = P                             |
|                                   |
|o1 : Polyhedron                    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : vertices P                    |
|                                   |
|o2 = | -3/2 3/2 0    0   0    0   ||
|     | 0    0   -3/2 3/2 0    0   ||
|     | 0    0   0    0   -3/2 3/2 ||
|                                   |
|              3       6            |
|o2 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ             |
+-----------------------------------+

Ways to use crossPolytope:
==========================

  * "crossPolytope(ZZ)"
  * "crossPolytope(ZZ,QQ)"
  * "crossPolytope(ZZ,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note crossPolytope: crossPolytope, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

