cyclicPolytope -- computes the d dimensional cyclic polytope with n vertices
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        P = cyclicPolytope(d,n)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, strictly positive
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, strictly positive
  * Outputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


The d-dimensional cyclicPolytope with n vertices is the convex hull of n points
on the moment curve in *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,^d. The moment curve is
defined by t -> (t,t^2,...,t^d) and the function takes the points {0,...,n-1}.
+----------------------------+
|i1 : P = cyclicPolytope(3,5)|
|                            |
|o1 = P                      |
|                            |
|o1 : Polyhedron             |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : vertices P             |
|                            |
|o2 = | 0 1 2 3  4  |        |
|     | 0 1 4 9  16 |        |
|     | 0 1 8 27 64 |        |
|                            |
|              3       5     |
|o2 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ      |
+----------------------------+

Ways to use cyclicPolytope:
===========================

  * "cyclicPolytope(ZZ,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note cyclicPolytope: cyclicPolytope, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

