directProduct(Fan,Fan) -- computes the direct product of two fans
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note directProduct: (Macaulay2Doc)directProduct,
  * Usage: 
        F = directProduct(F1,F2)
  * Inputs:
      * F1, an instance of the type *note Fan: Fan,
      * F2, an instance of the type *note Fan: Fan,
  * Outputs:
      * F, an instance of the type *note Fan: Fan,

Description
===========


The directProduct of two fans is the fan given by C = C1 x C2 for all cones C1
in F1 and C2 in F2 in the direct product of the ambient spaces.
+-------------------------------+
|i1 : F1 = normalFan hypercube 1|
|                               |
|o1 = F1                        |
|                               |
|o1 : Fan                       |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : F2 = normalFan hypercube 2|
|                               |
|o2 = F2                        |
|                               |
|o2 : Fan                       |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : F = directProduct(F1,F2)  |
|                               |
|o3 = F                         |
|                               |
|o3 : Fan                       |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : F == normalFan hypercube 3|
|                               |
|o4 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+


See also *note Fan * Fan: Fan _st Fan,.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note directProduct(Fan,Fan): directProduct_lpFan_cmFan_rp, -- computes the
    direct product of two fans
