dualCone --  computes the dual Cone
***********************************

  * Usage: 
        Cv = dualCone C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
  * Outputs:
      * Cv, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,

Description
===========


The dual cone of C in *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,^n is the cone in the dual
ambient space (*note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,^n)^*, given by {p in (*note QQ:
(Macaulay2Doc)QQ,^n)^* | p*c >= 0 for all c in C}.
+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2},{2,1}}|
|                                           |
|o1 = C                                     |
|                                           |
|o1 : Cone                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Cv = dualCone C                       |
|                                           |
|o2 = Cv                                    |
|                                           |
|o2 : Cone                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i3 : rays Cv                               |
|                                           |
|o3 = | 2  -1 |                             |
|     | -1 2  |                             |
|                                           |
|              2       2                    |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                     |
+-------------------------------------------+

