fan -- generates a Fan
**********************

  * Usage: 
        F = fan C 
        F = fan L
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, with elements of class *note
        Cone: Cone, or *note Fan: Fan,
  * Outputs:
      * F, an instance of the type *note Fan: Fan,

Description
===========


 If fan is applied to a *note Cone: Cone, it generates the *note Fan: Fan,
given by the Cone and all of its faces. If applied to a *note List:
(Macaulay2Doc)List, the list must only contain Cones and Fans in the same
ambient space. Then it adds the Cones in the List and the generating Cones of
the Fans in the List one by one to the Fan, checking each time if the new Cone
is compatible with the cones that have already been added, i.e. that the
intersection with each of them is a face of both Cones (intersection
condition).


If one of the cones is in the wrong ambient space, there will be an error and
no fan will be returned. If the intersection condition fails, there will also
be an error. The pairs of incompatible cones can be accessed with the function
*note incompCones: incompCones,.
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,-1},{0,-1}}  |
|                                               |
|o1 = C                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : Cone                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = fan C                                 |
|                                               |
|o2 = F                                         |
|                                               |
|o2 : Fan                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C1 = coneFromVData matrix {{1,0},{0,1}};  |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C2 = coneFromVData matrix {{0,-1},{1,-1}};|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = fan {C,C1,C2}                         |
|                                               |
|o5 = F                                         |
|                                               |
|o5 : Fan                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Ways to use fan:
================

  * "fan(Cone)"
  * "fan(List)"
  * "fan(Matrix,List)" -- see *note fan(Matrix,Matrix,List):
    fan_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_cmList_rp, -- Constructing a fan.
  * *note fan(Matrix,Matrix,List): fan_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_cmList_rp, --
    Constructing a fan.
  * "fan(Matrix,Matrix,Sequence)" -- see *note fan(Matrix,Matrix,List):
    fan_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_cmList_rp, -- Constructing a fan.
  * "fan(Matrix,Sequence)" -- see *note fan(Matrix,Matrix,List):
    fan_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_cmList_rp, -- Constructing a fan.
  * *note fan(PolyhedralComplex): fan_lpPolyhedralComplex_rp, -- Take the fan
    over a polyhedral complex

