fan(Matrix,Matrix,List) -- Constructing a fan.
**********************************************

  * Function: *note fan: fan,
  * Usage: 
        F = fan(M,N,L)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, Matrix containing the rays as
        columns.
      * N, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, Matrix containing generators
        of the lineality space as columns.
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, List containing lists with
        indices of the rays of the maximal cones.
  * Outputs:
      * F, an instance of the type *note Fan: Fan,, 

Description
===========

Basic constructor for fans that takes a matrix containing the rays of the fan
and a list of lists with the indices of the rays in the maximal cones.
Optionally one may provide a lineality space.

This constructor does not check well-definedness, see *note isWellDefined:
(Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,.



+----------------------------+
|i1 : M = matrix{{1,0},{0,1}}|
|                            |
|o1 = | 1 0 |                |
|     | 0 1 |                |
|                            |
|              2       2     |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ      |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : L = {{0,1}}            |
|                            |
|o2 = {{0, 1}}               |
|                            |
|o2 : List                   |
+----------------------------+
|i3 : F = fan(M,L)           |
|                            |
|o3 = F                      |
|                            |
|o3 : Fan                    |
+----------------------------+
|i4 : N = matrix{{1},{1}}    |
|                            |
|o4 = | 1 |                  |
|     | 1 |                  |
|                            |
|              2       1     |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ      |
+----------------------------+
|i5 : F1 = fan(M,N,L)        |
|                            |
|o5 = F1                     |
|                            |
|o5 : Fan                    |
+----------------------------+

