fVector -- computes the f-vector of a Cone, Polyhedron, Fan or PolyhedralComplex
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        f = fVector C 
        f = fVector P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note PolyhedralObject: PolyhedralObject,
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing the number of faces
        for each codimension

Description
===========


The i-th entry of the f-vector of P is the number of dimension i-1 faces of P,
so it starts with the number vertices, has dim(P)+1 entries, and the last entry
is 1 for P itself. It is the same for a Cone C.
