hilbertBasis -- computes the Hilbert basis of a Cone
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        HB = hilbertBasis C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing the elements of the
        Hilbert basis

Description
===========


The Hilbert basis of the cone C is computed by the Project-and-Lift-algorithm
by Raymond Hemmecke (see below). It computes a Hilbert basis of the cone modulo
the lineality space, so it returns the list of one column matrices that give
the Hilbert basis of the Cone if one adds the basis of the lineality space and
its negative. For the Project-and-Lift-algorithm see:


Raymond Hemmecke's (see http://www.hemmecke.de/raymond/ ) On the computation of
Hilbert bases of cones, in A. M. Cohen, X.-S. Gao, and N. Takayama, editors,
Mathematical Software, ICMS 2002, pages 307317. World Scientific, 2002.
+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2},{2,1}}|
|                                           |
|o1 = C                                     |
|                                           |
|o1 : Cone                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : hilbertBasis C                        |
|                                           |
|o2 = {| 1 |, | 1 |, | 2 |}                 |
|      | 1 |  | 2 |  | 1 |                  |
|                                           |
|o2 : List                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+


Beginning with Macaulay2 version 1.24.11, this method calls the internal
function rawHilbertBasis which calls the C++ library *note libnormaliz:
(Macaulay2Doc)normaliz,.

See also
========

  * *note hilbertBasis(Matrix): (FourTiTwo)hilbertBasis_lpMatrix_rp, --
    calculates the Hilbert basis of the cone; invokes "hilbert" from 4ti2

Ways to use hilbertBasis:
=========================

  * "hilbertBasis(Cone)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note hilbertBasis: hilbertBasis, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

