File: Polyhedra.info, Node: hyperplanes, Next: imageFan, Prev: hypercube, Up: Top

hyperplanes -- computes the defining hyperplanes of a Cone or a Polyhedron
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = hyperplanes C 
        (N,w) = hyperplanes P
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with entries over *note QQ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
      * w, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with entries over *note QQ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)QQ, and only one column

Description
===========


hyperplanes returns the defining affine hyperplanes for a polyhedron P. The
output is (N,w), where the source of N has the dimension of the ambient space
of P and w is a one column matrix in the target space of N such that P = {p in
H | N*p = w} where H is the intersection of the defining affine half-spaces.


 For a cone C the output is the matrix N, that is the same matrix as before but
w is omitted since it is 0, so C = {c in H | N*c = 0} and H is the intersection
of the defining linear half-spaces.


Please see *note V- and H-representation: V- and H-representation, on the
conventions we use for cones and polyhedra.
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = stdSimplex 2                                  |
|                                                       |
|o1 = P                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o1 : Polyhedron                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : hyperplanes P                                     |
|                                                       |
|o2 = (| 1 1 1 |, | 1 |)                                |
|                                                       |
|o2 : Sequence                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1,2,4},{2,3,5},{3,4,6}}|
|                                                       |
|o3 = C                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o3 : Cone                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hyperplanes C                                     |
|                                                       |
|o4 = | -1 2 -1 |                                       |
|                                                       |
|              1       3                                |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use hyperplanes:
========================

  * "hyperplanes(Cone)"
  * "hyperplanes(Polyhedron)"

