        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if p lies in the relative interior of the
        Cone/Polyhedron, *note false: (Macaulay2Doc)false, otherwise

Description
===========


inInterior checks if the smallest face of the *note Cone: Cone, or the *note
Polyhedron: Polyhedron, containing p is the *note Cone: Cone, or the *note
Polyhedron: Polyhedron, itself. For this the number of rows of p must equal the
ambient dimension of the second argument.
+-----------------------------+
|i1 : P = cyclicPolytope(3,5) |
|                             |
|o1 = P                       |
|                             |
|o1 : Polyhedron              |
+-----------------------------+
