minkowskiSum --  computes the Minkowski sum of two convex objects
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Q = minkowskiSum(X,Y)
  * Inputs:
      * X, *note Cone: Cone, or *note Polyhedron: Polyhedron,
      * Y, *note Cone: Cone, or *note Polyhedron: Polyhedron,
  * Outputs:
      * Q, *note Cone: Cone, or *note Polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


The Minkowski sum of X and Y is the polyhedron X + Y = {x + y | x in X, y in
Y}. If X and Y are both cones, then their Minkowski sum is their positive hull,
which is a cone, so the output is a *note Cone: Cone,. Otherwise the output is
a *note Polyhedron: Polyhedron,. X and Y have to lie in the same ambient space.
+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P1 = convexHull matrix {{0,1,-1},{0,-1,-1}}|
|                                                |
|o1 = P1                                         |
|                                                |
|o1 : Polyhedron                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P2 = convexHull matrix {{0,1,-1},{0,1,1}}  |
|                                                |
|o2 = P2                                         |
|                                                |
|o2 : Polyhedron                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = minkowskiSum(P1,P2)                    |
|                                                |
|o3 = Q                                          |
|                                                |
|o3 : Polyhedron                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : vertices Q                                 |
|                                                |
|o4 = | -2 2 -1 1  -1 1 |                        |
|     | 0  0 -1 -1 1  1 |                        |
|                                                |
|              2       6                         |
|o4 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                          |
+------------------------------------------------+


See also *note Cone + Cone: Cone + Cone,, *note Cone + Polyhedron: Cone +
Polyhedron,, *note Polyhedron + Cone: Polyhedron + Cone,, and *note Polyhedron
+ Cone: Polyhedron + Cone,.

