mixedVolume -- computes the mixed volume of a list of polytope
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        v = mixedVolume L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing n polytopes in n-space
  * Outputs:
      * v, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the mixed volume

Description
===========


Let $P_1,...,P_n$ be polytopes in $n$-space. Then the volume of the Minkowski
sum $\lambda_1 P_1 + ... + \lambda_n P_n$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree
$n$ in nonnegative variables $\lambda_1,...,\lambda_n$. The coefficient
Vol$(P_1,...,P_n)$ of $\lambda_1\lambda_2 ... \lambda_n$ is called the mixed
volume of $P_1,...,P_n$. For example, the number of toric solutions to a
generic system of /$n$ polynomial equations on $n$-space amounts to the mixed
volume of the corresponding Newton polytopes.


The function mixedVolume takes the *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, L with $n$
polytopes in $n$-space and computes their mixed Volume by using the algorithm
by Ioannis Z. Emiris in his paper Mixed Volume Implementation (see
http://www.nag.co.uk/projects/frisco/frisco/reports/d33421.ps ). Note that this
function computes an upper bound by using a random lifting. To reassure the
result run the function until it returns the same result.


CAVEAT: So far the input is not checked so use the function with care!
+------------------------+
|i1 : P = crossPolytope 2|
|                        |
|o1 = P                  |
|                        |
|o1 : Polyhedron         |
+------------------------+
|i2 : Q = hypercube 2    |
|                        |
|o2 = Q                  |
|                        |
|o2 : Polyhedron         |
+------------------------+
|i3 : mixedVolume {P,Q}  |
|                        |
|o3 = 8                  |
|                        |
|o3 : QQ                 |
+------------------------+

Ways to use mixedVolume:
========================

  * "mixedVolume(List)"

For the programmer
==================

