newtonPolytope -- computes the Newton polytope of a polynomial
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        P = newtonPolytope f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,
  * Outputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


The newtonPolytope of f is the convex hull of its exponent vectors in n-space,
where n is the number of variables in the ring.


Consider the Vandermond determinant in 3 variables:
+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c]                       |
|                                         |
|o1 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                      |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = (a-b)*(a-c)*(b-c)               |
|                                         |
|      2       2    2     2       2      2|
|o2 = a b - a*b  - a c + b c + a*c  - b*c |
|                                         |
|o2 : R                                   |
+-----------------------------------------+


If we compute the Newton polytope we get a hexagon in QQ^3.
+-------------------------+
|i3 : P = newtonPolytope f|
|                         |
|o3 = P                   |
|                         |
|o3 : Polyhedron          |
+-------------------------+

Ways to use newtonPolytope:
===========================

  * "newtonPolytope(RingElement)"

For the programmer
==================

