Polyhedron + Cone -- computes the Minkowski sum of a polyhedron and a cone
**************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note +: (Macaulay2Doc)+,
  * Usage: 
        Q = P + C
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
  * Outputs:
      * Q, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


Computes the Minkowski sum of P and C. This is the polyhedron P + C = {p + c |
p in P, c in C}. Note that P and C have to lie in the same ambient space.


See also *note minkowskiSum: minkowskiSum,.
+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = hypercube 2                   |
|                                       |
|o1 = P                                 |
|                                       |
|o1 : Polyhedron                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = coneFromVData matrix {{1},{2}}|
|                                       |
|o2 = C                                 |
|                                       |
|o2 : Cone                              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = P + C                         |
|                                       |
|o3 = Q                                 |
|                                       |
|o3 : Polyhedron                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : (vertices Q,rays Q)               |
|                                       |
|o4 = (| -1 1  -1 |, | 1 |)             |
|      | -1 -1 1  |  | 2 |              |
|                                       |
|o4 : Sequence                          |
+---------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Polyhedron + Cone: Polyhedron + Cone, -- computes the Minkowski sum
    of a polyhedron and a cone
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

