Polyhedron + Polyhedron -- computes the Minkowski sum of two polyhedra
**********************************************************************

  * Operator: *note +: (Macaulay2Doc)+,
  * Usage: 
        Q = P1 + P2
  * Inputs:
      * P1, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
      * P2, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
  * Outputs:
      * Q, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,

Description
===========


Computes the Minkowski sum of P1 and P2.This is the polyhedron P1 + P2 = {x + y
| x in P1, y in P2}. Note that P1 and P2 have to lie in the same ambient space.


See also *note minkowskiSum: minkowskiSum,.
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P1 = convexHull matrix {{1,0,0},{0,1,0}}  |
|                                               |
|o1 = P1                                        |
|                                               |
|o1 : Polyhedron                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P2 = convexHull matrix {{-1,0,0},{0,-1,0}}|
|                                               |
|o2 = P2                                        |
|                                               |
|o2 : Polyhedron                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : P = P1 + P2                               |
|                                               |
|o3 = P                                         |
|                                               |
|o3 : Polyhedron                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : vertices P                                |
|                                               |
|o4 = | -1 1 0  1  0 -1 |                       |
|     | 0  0 -1 -1 1 1  |                       |
|                                               |
|              2       6                        |
|o4 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
