proximum -- computes the proximum of the Polyhedron/Cone to a point in euclidean metric
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        q = proximum(p,P) 
        q = proximum(p,C)
  * Inputs:
      * p, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,,  over *note ZZ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ, with only one column
        representing a point
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,
  * Outputs:
      * q, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,,  over *note QQ:
        (Macaulay2Doc)QQ, with only one column representing the closest point

Description
===========


For a point p and a Polyhedron P or a Cone C, proximum computes the point in P
or C with minimal euclidean distance to p.
+-----------------------------+
|i1 : P = crossPolytope 3     |
|                             |
|o1 = P                       |
|                             |
|o1 : Polyhedron              |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : p = matrix {{1},{2},{3}}|
|                             |
|o2 = | 1 |                   |
|     | 2 |                   |
|     | 3 |                   |
|                             |
|              3       1      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ       |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : q = proximum(p,P)       |
|                             |
|o3 = | 0 |                   |
|     | 0 |                   |
|     | 1 |                   |
|                             |
|              3       1      |
|o3 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ       |
+-----------------------------+

