tailCone -- computes the tail/recession cone of a polyhedron
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = tailCone P
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: Polyhedron,
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: Cone,

Description
===========


Every polyhedron P can be uniquely decomposed into the sum of a polytope and a
cone, the tail or recession cone of P. Thus, it is the cone generated by the
non-compact part, i.e. the rays and the lineality space of P. If P is a
polytope then the tail cone is the origin in the ambient space of P.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = polyhedronFromHData(matrix{{-1,0},{1,0},{0,-1},{-1,-1},{1,-1}},     |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = P                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Polyhedron                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|matrix{{2},{2},{-1},{0},{0}})                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = tailCone P                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = C                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Cone                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : rays C                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | 0 |                                                                   |
|     | 1 |                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|              2       1                                                      |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

